WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.370
Kyou Kai...

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.040
Worried about Sho?

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:56.450
Shou Sa said it meant we
wouldn't be fightin' 'em anytime soon,

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.870
but I dunno...

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.620
I just...

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.410
I just can't take on Ri Boku soon enough.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.410
To get revenge?

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.790
It's a little different from <i>your</i> revenge, though.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.910
We're both settling old scores.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.580
Let's get our revenges over with, eh?

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.700
Yes.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.580
What is it?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.080
The post-horse is coming.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.120
"The Quiet Battlefield"

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.500
Hey, messenger man! Where've you been?!

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.120
Go on ahead!
Say your names and they'll let you pass!

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.120
Got it!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.870
Ri Boku--in Kanyou? What the hell is going on?

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:50.370
That man has made a downright mess of things!

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.200
Acting without His Highness's permission...

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.830
It is an outrage
that will <i>not</i> be tolerated, Ryo Fui!

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.580
Calm yourself, Shou Bun Kun!

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.750
How can I calm myself in the midst of all this?!

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.790
It's crucial that we
consider what the man is thinking!

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.830
Thinking? He isn't thinking at all!

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:11.700
I come back for a rare visit,
and look at all the commotion you've caused.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.870
Your little prank is a bit much, Minister.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.950
Ryo Fui was once a merchant
who traveled from kingdom to kingdom.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.700
Some ten years earlier, while living in Sho,

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.370
he made the acquaintance
of a young man named Shun Pei Kun.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.250
A short time before the upheaval presently at hand,

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:38.700
Ryo Fui wrote a letter
to Shun Pei Kun seemingly out of the blue,

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.660
proposing that the two
work together to rebuild relations

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.660
between the Kingdoms of Chin and Sho.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.910
Having gained favor with King Tou Jou
and wanting to please him,

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.660
Lord Shun Pei Kun paid a secret visit to Chin.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:57.410
There, of all things,
he was abducted by Ryo Fui,

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:03.750
who then sent a ransom note
demanding a visit from the chancellor

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.290
in return for the hostage.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.160
Summon Ri Boku!

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.910
You can't do this, my lord!
You may as well be offering yourself up to die!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:20.450
Kaine is right--the Ou Ki
incident has Chin up in arms!

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:26.040
What's our king thinking, swapping
Ri Boku for a nobody like Lord Shun Pei Kun...

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.290
Please wait, Ri Boku.
The Ministers are reasoning with His Highness.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.500
General Kou Son Ryuu!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:39.130
Such persuasion is futile!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:39.130
"Kou Son Ryuu, General of Sho"

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:40.200
At this stage, our king will not
entertain any other opinion on the matter.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.370
Chin certainly has hit us where it hurts.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.200
Ryo Shi understands our king's temperament all too well.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.950
Will you go?

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:58.200
I've been told that to refuse
is to be beheaded for treason.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.000
You're risking your life.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.580
I'm risking it either way. Besides...

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.700
it's a good chance to see Kanyou
and this Ryo Fui fellow for myself.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.950
Three monarchs ago, King Burei
once risked his life to ride into Kanyou.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:23.830
I've heard that story.
King Burei pretended to be a Sho messenger,

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:27.160
Chou Sho, to gain an audience with King Sho.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.200
Is Ri Boku looking to do the same?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:35.250
But <i>my</i> host has practically
foisted this opportunity onto me.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.040
How can I not accept?

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.370
I shall ready the troops and accompany you.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.830
That's reassuring.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.330
Ri Boku will reach Kanyou at any moment!

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:51.250
How does the Minister of the Right
propose we handle this?!

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.830
And where is the army?

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.620
Stationed at the south gate. Minister's orders!

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.870
What?! But if worst comes to worst...

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:02.950
Dammit! Where <i>is</i> the minister, anyway?!

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:04.450
Silence!

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:08.450
What's the use in fussing
and fighting at this late hour?

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:12.540
You shall welcome Ri Boku
and wait for the minister! Understood?

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:17.540
Ryo Fui, what were you
thinking with this stunt of yours?

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:24.580
May I, my lord? They're running riot down there.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.330
Ri Shi...

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.790
How do you take this Ri Boku fellow?

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.830
Sir. His intelligence-handling in that last battle

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:34.870
"Ri Shi: One of Ryo Fui's 
Four Pillars (inner circle)"

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.790
was almost beyond belief.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.200
As a tactician, he has broken the mold...

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.700
...and he's all the more dangerous for it.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.290
That's not what I meant.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:48.950
I was born in Kan, in Yo Teki,
and rose to my rank from a mere merchant.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:52.370
I still have a keen eye for quality.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:56.580
Now then, what kind of man is this Ri Boku?

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:04.250
Everyone's runnin' around like crazy.
Feels like a whole other palace!

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.450
Hurry! This way!

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.370
S-Shou Hei Kun?!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.700
Thank you for coming all this way.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:24.450
We have heard of your exploits
on the front lines, Shin of the Hi Shin Unit.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.750
Hey! Bow your head!

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.540
<i>You're</i> the one who called me here?

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:34.160
Are you mad? This personage
is the army's high commander!

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:35.040
Enough.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.790
We three shall speak alone. Leave us.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.620
Y-Yes, my lord!

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.410
Choose your words wisely, Shin.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:46.250
I speak to you now
not as one of Ryo Shi's Four Pillars,

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.120
but as the high commander of Chin.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.040
Ri Boku has entered Kanyou.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.540
Here we go.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:59.000
Ri Boku, huh? I wonder if Kaine's here, too.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.200
Maybe.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:05.000
Aren't they scared,
going smack into the heart of enemy territory?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.000
They must be petrified.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.910
But I'm wondering about something else.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.410
Like what?

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:16.950
I tried looking at it
from my teacher's point of view.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:19.330
Who summoned Ri Boku? The Minister of the Right did.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.330
Even I am not aware
of the minister's true intentions,

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.080
but we must be prepared.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.080
Prepared?!

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:30.410
Disguise yourselves as sentries
and sneak into the meeting.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:37.660
If the unthinkable happens
with Chin's fate in the balance...

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.080
On my signal,

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.330
cut Ri Boku down!

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:46.580
...my teacher is sure
to issue a decisive command.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:50.200
Ah, yes! A Shin and
a Kyou Kai of the Hi Shin Unit

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.290
have been summoned here from the front lines.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:56.580
Ka Ryo Ten, weren't you and Shin--

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.830
No way...!

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.580
You're tellin' me to become an assassin.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.450
I am.

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:07.830
No way!

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.540
Who would ever stoop to such a cowardly trick?!

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:17.950
Why, I'd be too ashamed
to look General Ou Ki in the eye!

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.830
If you won't, another will.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.450
M-Mou Bu...

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.420
"Mou Bu: One of Ryo Fui's 
Four Pillars (inner circle)"

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:34.700
Tou--and the combat commanders!

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:36.950
Shin...

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:41.660
My calling you here
was the smallest kindness I could offer

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:44.410
to the one who received Ou Ki's poleax.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.540
I do not know why,
but the Minister has permitted

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.370
the Sho contingent to remain armed.

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:53.580
It has taken a strange form,

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.830
but at this point, it can only be

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.330
war.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.960
"Ei Sei"

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:12.450
I am Ri Boku, chancellor of Sho.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:15.290
And I am Chin's Minister of the Right, Ryo Fui.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:29.580
This guy? This is Ri Boku?

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.750
His looks say one thing...
but the powerful stink of war about 'im

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:35.500
is tellin' a whole other story.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:41.540
Indeed, Ri Boku the military man
has been on countless battlefields.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:45.290
It was that experience that supported his strategy

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.450
and made it possible to lay Ou Ki low!

00:10:54.620 --> 00:11:00.910
Seems Sho is overwhelmed
by the greatness of their own minister!

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:05.000
We meet at last, Chancellor Ri Boku.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:08.910
It's a pleasure, Minister Ryo Fui.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.870
They're laughin'!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.410
Truly, thank you for coming, Chancellor.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.120
How is Kantan nowadays?

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.200
It must have grown
quite a bit since I was last there.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.500
I stay in the frontier lands,
so I can't speak to any changes,

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.200
but I'm sure you must be right.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.120
Kantan... That takes me back.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:42.330
A capital city like Kanyou,
but differing in its opulence.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:46.000
Why, Kantan could be
the capital of the whole Middle Kingdom.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.160
Here it is some dozen years after having left Sho,

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:52.120
with you now minister of the great land of Chin.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.330
You must be terribly resourceful.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:59.410
Sho may be my second home,
but I am now a minister of Chin, its enemy.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:02.910
What's more, now that
we are fighting my old homeland,

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:06.750
its people must look upon me with contempt.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:10.660
Not at all. Improving one's
station by serving different nations

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.910
is simply the way of war.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:17.120
On the contrary, Sho rejoices
to have brought forth such a great man.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.080
That's good to hear.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:23.830
And you, Ri Boku--you have been
chancellor for only a year or so.

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.450
How are you finding it?

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:30.830
Is it difficult being so popular
after such success in last year's battle?

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.040
If I may be frank...

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.620
In a word, it is stifling.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.910
I have never been the leader type,
so to be entrusted with a kingdom

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:43.410
and its people is proving a terrific burden.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.830
And I am not used to the elegance of cities.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.660
I would like to return to the frontier,

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:52.120
defend the land with my friends, start a family,

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:56.080
tend sheep... and grow old, in time.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:59.160
That's the kind of peaceful life I want to lead.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.040
You jest. To think a national hero as yourself

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:06.330
would nurse such a disheartening dream!

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:11.700
I expected the man who finished
Ou Ki to be bigger than that.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.370
Quite the opposite.
It's because I am a small man

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.410
that I am desperate
to formulate these cunning strategies.

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:18.950
You may call it craven,

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:22.200
but I will do whatever
it takes to remain unharmed.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:27.790
Since becoming chancellor,
I have come to envy daring men like you.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:28.830
Then again,

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:32.580
if I were daring, I would probably
never have gone after Ou Ki.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.450
I see! So you're a coward!

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:42.830
So that's it!

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:47.120
Now... shall we move onto the matter at hand?

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:51.450
You <i>will</i> be dying here.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.540
What?!

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:56.540
If you were an ordinary tactician,
you would not be worth killing.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:59.250
But you are not ordinary.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:05.620
Call yourself a coward if you wish,
but that's no way to show your greatness.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.000
It is clear that you are not greedy.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.120
As the very embodiment of greed myself,

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.540
I tend to view such people as rather trivial.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:17.250
Yet somehow you
come across as frightfully powerful.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.830
And so, I shall kill you.

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:27.250
Surely this was not an
entirely unforeseen development for you.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:32.370
So, Ri Boku the Genius,
how shall we send you to your death, hmm?

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:39.500
I come bearing a gift, of course.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:46.160
An empty gesture--unless it is
more valuable than your head.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.500
I know.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.580
That's his gift? A map?!

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.500
No, it's not that.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:04.290
Do you know anything
about this, General Kou Son Ryuu?

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.410
Nothing.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:11.290
Now, if you'll permit me
to speak as Chin's strategist...

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:14.040
I'm listening.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:19.660
The Middle Kingdom is in
the age of the Seven Warring States.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:23.580
But these seven kingdoms differ in might.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:27.160
There's Chin, which greatly expanded
its power during King Sho's reign,

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:30.290
and So, whose land spans
fully half of the Middle Kingdom.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:35.700
These two are at the top,
and Sho, Gi, Se and En are in the middle.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.700
Kan is at the bottom,
with its smaller size and weaker army.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:44.660
These seven kingdoms maintain an exquisite balance,

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:48.290
fighting one another for nearly 200 years now.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:52.830
But if we here in Chin truly
want to conquer the Middle Kingdom,

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:56.660
we must do our utmost
to stamp out these other nations, one by one.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:16:01.160
First we turn to weaker Kan.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:05.370
Now, Kan is highly significant for Chin.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:10.750
Kan is blocking Chin's path
to the rest of the Middle Kingdom.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:15.870
Until Chin destroys Kan,
our dream will never be realized.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.790
Now, here's the rub:

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.540
The weak Kingdom of Kan will never fall.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:29.330
If Chin tries to take it down,
Sho and Gi will muster their huge armies

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:31.580
and send reinforcements into Kan.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:32.750
What?!

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:38.580
Gi and Sho see Kan
as the shield keeping Chin in check.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:42.660
Without Kan, Chin's sword
would soon be at their necks,

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:45.250
and they <i>will</i> jump in to defend Kan.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:50.290
So Kan shouldn't be
Chin's first target. Go after Gi.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:55.330
Give Gi a thorough beating
until they lack the strength to help Kan.

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:59.750
Once you've done that,
only Sho can come to Kan's aid...

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:04.200
but this is where Chancellor Ri Boku vows

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.540
that Sho will provide Kan no assistance.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.200
There are strings attached.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:17.790
I shall go back to being Chancellor Ri Boku of Sho.

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:22.620
My lovely land of Sho
is nestled between En and Chin,

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:25.250
with whom we have a storied past.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:30.290
Sho's greatest challenge
is having to divide its power between them.

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:34.540
Therefore, we will henceforth
focus on our battle with En.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:40.040
During this time,
Chin will promise not to lay a finger on Sho.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:47.000
W-Wait... Is that...

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.000
You mean...

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.450
Yes: a Chin-Sho alliance.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.450
An... alliance?

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.750
Sho and Chin--

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.450
allies?

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.120
Who are you kidding?!

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:07.790
Why should we enter
into an alliance with the likes of you?!

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:11.650
"Roku O Mi: Tou
 Army General"

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:11.790
Enough of this farce. Tell him, Minister!

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.660
On behalf of the late General Ou Ki, I, Roku O Mi,

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.290
will knock every last one
of your heads off your shoulders!

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:21.250
Know your place! This is no farce.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:26.410
I understand how you feel...
but soldiers are not welcome here.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:30.290
"Tou: Chin Army General
(former Ou Ki Army lieutenant)"

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:38.830
This is surprising, indeed.
For Sho to propose an alliance with Chin...

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:43.830
Killing Ri Boku here would cost
Chin the trust of the other six nations,

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.410
and there are many drawbacks
to remaining independent.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:49.250
This is not a bad idea at all.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:52.000
We've found common ground, Ryo Fui!

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:53.540
I refuse!

00:18:56.290 --> 00:18:58.910
He... He said no?!

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:07.000
Of course Ri Boku
would come proposing an alliance.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:12.120
Allying with Sho at this juncture
would greatly benefit both kingdoms.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:15.790
However, as for Ri Boku,
the bearer of this proposal?

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:19.660
You are Sho's one and only treasure.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:24.410
In comparing the value
of your head to that of this alliance,

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.160
I find that, by the smallest of margins,

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:29.660
your head is the greater prize.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:33.370
But that is why there is
leeway in these negotiations.

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.620
Negotiations?

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:38.370
Hmm, let's see here...

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.040
All right, Ri Boku--

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.790
How about we take one of your castles?

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.250
Castles?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.660
Did he say a castle?

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:55.000
You... mean for me to simply... hand over a castle?

00:19:55.000 --> 00:20:02.120
I do! I know the perfect spot,
where I often traveled in my merchant days!

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:06.160
In... Kankou, was it?

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:08.830
Kankou?! Ri Boku, my lord!

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:14.790
Kankou--is that the Kankou
in the southwest of Sho?

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.660
Undoubtedly so.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:18.370
Thanks to changing borders,

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:22.370
Kankou has experienced
a recent surge in military importance.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:25.870
With that in mind,
Ri Boku started boosting the area's defense

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:31.660
as soon as he became chancellor,
building a giant castle at its center

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.290
that we are told is near completion.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:38.120
If we attempted to capture that castle,

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:43.120
how many soldiers' lives,
how much money, how much time would it take?

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:47.950
To simply demand
the castle in Kankou is utterly mad.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.410
Is Ryo Fui...

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:57.750
That's our minister for you--
he drives a hard bargain!

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:03.250
Surely he would be satisfied
with the common ground of a Chin-Sho alliance.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:09.910
It's his merchant spirit
that's making him squeeze a little harder.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:13.790
Now then, it's down to Ri Boku.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:19.000
Can he lower the minister's asking price?

00:21:20.620 --> 00:21:24.290
It's not for me to decide if you may have a castle.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:27.750
--If I may return to Sho and get the king's--
--You may not.

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:31.750
Say you will give it to us and the king will allow it.

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:34.000
After all, we have Shun Pei Kun--

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:38.660
and the king wants him back
badly enough to risk your life.

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:43.250
Then perhaps you would
consider a castle other than Kankou...

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:48.410
That one is still being built,
and it's so close to the Gi border

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.120
that it is hardly convenient for Chin.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.080
No. I want Kankou.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:55.080
It would take ten lesser castles to equal that one.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:59.950
Take heed, Ri Boku: In all my sales negotiations,

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:04.540
I have never budged from
my bottom line--not a single coin!

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:10.290
That's enough.
No more trying to outwit one another.

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:14.910
The cards are on the table.
Your choice is simple:

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:18.500
Give us Kankou Castle
and enter into a Chin-Sho alliance

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:23.160
or you and your companions
will be executed where you stand.

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:25.290
One or the other.

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:31.120
Now, Chancellor Ri Boku... Your answer?

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:46.830
Sadly, I have no chance of beating your price.

00:22:46.830 --> 00:22:49.160
Kankou Castle is yours.

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:54.250
Excellent! The Chin-Sho alliance is concluded!

00:22:56.540 --> 00:22:58.620
Shouldn't we be raising hell?

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:03.120
Even if we did... the stakes are too high.

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.370
Ryo Fui was right:
This is no place for soldiers.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:12.910
So that's the monster you're fighting, Sei...

00:23:48.830 --> 00:23:51.750
<i>What do you think?</i>

00:23:51.750 --> 00:23:54.830
<i>Why would the voice that melted into the sky</i>

00:23:54.830 --> 00:23:59.450
<i>Peel away and disappear?</i>

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.790
<i>Just a single word</i>

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:06.830
<i>If that's all you'd say</i>

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:11.700
<i>What kind of word would you choose?</i>

00:24:12.540 --> 00:24:15.910
<i>Holding my breath and making sure</i>

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:18.870
<i>The heartbeat can't wait</i>

00:24:18.870 --> 00:24:24.830
<i>If I let go of your hand, I'll want even more</i>

00:24:24.830 --> 00:24:28.450
<i>And so I keep on doing this</i>

00:24:28.450 --> 00:24:30.910
<i>Not allowing myself to stop</i>

00:24:30.910 --> 00:24:35.700
<i>Because I'm still searching for answers</i>

00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:39.370
<i>I want you to tell me</i>

00:24:41.700 --> 00:24:46.200
<i>Before you melt away into the sky</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:57.970
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:01.660 --> 00:25:07.020
"A Tempestuous Feast"
